title: "The UOHF Human Function Capacity System, Version 1.0: Unified Definitions of 18 Core and 104 Specific Human Functional Capacities"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Che
    given-names: Lei
    email: dlehche@gmail.com
    affiliation: "MoveTips Technology (Beijing) Co., Ltd."
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-08-17
url: "https://github.com/dlehche/Unified-Ontology-Of-Human-Function/tree/main/papers/capacity-system"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dlehche/Unified-Ontology-Of-Human-Function"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
abstract: >-
  Version 1.0 of the UOHF Human Function Capacity System is a public repository
  preprint that defines a citable catalogue of 18 core human functional
  capacities and 104 fine-grained capacity objects. The public expression
  "specific capacity" covers formally typed SUBCAPACITY and CAPACITY_COMPONENT
  objects subordinate to their CORE_CAPACITY. The catalogue is whole-person
  centered, source-traceable, versioned, and type-audited to distinguish
  capacities from structures, processes, tasks, measurements, episodic
  performances, and states. Catalogue inclusion does not itself assert
  production-runtime release.
keywords:
  - human function
  - UOHF
  - Unified Ontology of Human Function
  - human functional capacity
  - whole person
  - functional engagement
  - ontology
